210w|n|The basis or foundation of a thing; especially, a horizontal piece, as a timber, which forms the lower member of a frame, or supports a structure; as, the sills of a house, of a bridge, of a loom, and the like. ; The timber or stone at the foot of a door; the threshold. ; The timber or stone on which a window frame stands; or, the lowest piece in a window frame. ; The floor of a gallery or passage in a mine. ; A piece of timber across the bottom of a canal lock for the gates to shut against. ; The shaft or thill of a carriage. ; A young herring.	n:2go2,102,4~2go2,102,4
