21cl|v|A thin, weak glue used in various trades, as in painting, bookbinding, paper making, etc. ; Any viscous substance, as gilder's varnish. ; To cover with size; to prepare with size. ; To fix the standard of. ; To adjust or arrange according to size or bulk. ; To take the height of men, in order to place them in the ranks according to their stature. ; To sift, as pieces of ore or metal, in order to separate the finer from the coarser parts. ; To swell; to increase the bulk of. ; To bring or adjust anything exactly to a required dimension, as by cutting. ; To take greater size; to increase in size. ; To order food or drink from the buttery; hence, to enter a score, as upon the buttery book.	o:1e9t,29,2;fh4,6,1~1e9t,29,2;fh4,6,1	s:u8g,75,191;1za6,68,20;26q4,20,3;adk,19,2;1niq,14,5;1ljz,12,1;v6h,8,2;23jq,3,2;2go2,3,2;100k,2,7~u8g,75,191;1za6,68,20;100k,2,7;1niq,14,5;26q4,20,3;v6h,8,2;23jq,3,2;2go2,3,2;adk,19,2;1ljz,12,1
